+
+> Best AI tools for real estate agents in 2026 are increasingly open source, self-hostable, and customizable. This list curates verified GitHub repositories that can help agents and brokerages build lead capture assistants, searchable listing knowledge bases, document pipelines, media workflows, and valuation models without depending on proprietary SaaS lock-in.
+
+## Table of Contents
+- [TL;DR](#tldr)
+- [Why This List](#why-this-list)
+- [Open Source Tools](#open-source-tools)
+- [FAQ](#faq)
+- [Contributing](#contributing)
+- [License](#license)
+
+## TL;DR
+- **Best visual workflow builder:** [Langflow](https://github.com/langflow-ai/langflow) for agent copilots, lead-routing flows, and retrieval chains.
+- **Best all-in-one self-hosted workspace:** [AnythingLLM](https://github.com/Mintplex-Labs/anything-llm) for private brokerage knowledge bases and local document Q&A.
+- **Best RAG application stack:** [LlamaIndex](https://github.com/run-llama/llama_index) plus [Qdrant](https://github.com/qdrant/qdrant) for listing, neighborhood, and policy search.
+- **Best document ingestion set:** [Docling](https://github.com/docling-project/docling), [Unstructured](https://github.com/Unstructured-IO/unstructured), and [OCRmyPDF](https://github.com/ocrmypdf/OCRmyPDF).
+- **Best listing-media stack:** [ComfyUI](https://github.com/Comfy-Org/ComfyUI), [Fooocus](https://github.com/lllyasviel/Fooocus), and [Real-ESRGAN](https://github.com/xinntao/Real-ESRGAN).
+
+## Why This List
+Open source matters for real estate because the most useful AI systems usually need access to proprietary brokerage data: listing notes, transaction docs, CRM exports, neighborhood comps, photos, and call transcripts. Public GitHub repositories let agents and technical operators inspect the code, self-host the stack, control data residency, and combine multiple tools into a workflow that fits a local market.
+
+This list focuses only on tools with public GitHub repositories. There were very few truly real-estate-specific repositories, so the list honestly broadens to reusable open source AI building blocks that real estate agents can adapt for lead qualification, listing content, transaction paperwork, media production, and forecasting.
+
+## Open Source Tools
+
+### AI Assistants, Lead Capture, and Client Communication
+
+#### [Langflow](https://github.com/langflow-ai/langflow)
+> **Description:** Langflow describes itself as a platform for building and deploying AI-powered agents and workflows with a visual authoring experience, playground, API deployment, MCP server support, observability integrations, and support for major LLMs and vector databases. For real estate teams, that makes it a strong fit for lead-intake assistants, listing Q&A flows, buyer qualification pipelines, and internal brokerage copilots without starting from a blank codebase. **GitHub verification:** last commit date Mar 23, 2026, stars count 146k, primary language Python, license type MIT.
