+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for real estate agents in 2026?
+If you need a practical starting stack, use Langflow or Flowise for agent workflows, LlamaIndex plus Qdrant for knowledge retrieval, Docling plus OCRmyPDF for paperwork, and ComfyUI plus Real-ESRGAN for listing-media production. For pricing and forecasting, start with PyCaret or AutoGluon before moving to LightGBM or XGBoost.
+
+### Are there any truly real-estate-specific open source AI repos on GitHub?
+Very few. That is the main gap this research surfaced. Most useful projects are general open source AI building blocks that can be adapted to real estate. That is why this list focuses on verified GitHub repositories that solve concrete agent problems instead of pretending there is a large market of mature niche repos.
+
+### Can I self-host these AI tools for a brokerage or team?
+Most of the repositories here are designed for self-hosting, local development, or private deployment. That is one of the main advantages for brokerages handling client data, contracts, and internal knowledge. Always review the repository license and security posture before production use.
+
+### Which open source AI tools help with listing descriptions and content marketing?
+For copy generation and reusable workflows, start with Langflow, Flowise, crewAI, and LiteLLM. For image-centric marketing work, ComfyUI, InvokeAI, Stable Diffusion WebUI, Fooocus, and Real-ESRGAN are the most relevant picks in this list.
+
+### Which GitHub tools help real estate agents process contracts and disclosures?
+Docling, Unstructured, OCRmyPDF, paperless-ngx, and Tesseract OCR are the strongest document-processing entries here. Combined with a retrieval layer such as LlamaIndex, Haystack, or Qdrant, they can power searchable transaction archives and compliance assistants.
+
+### What is the best open source AI stack for private listing and CRM search?
